WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.420
Clash at Demon Head.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:06.860
Can a one-man engine of destruction prevent mankind's extinction?

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.560
Clash at Demon Head.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:30.820
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:31.840
I'm Mike.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.200
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.980
Guys, who has the better title?

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.940
The Terminator or the Engine of Destruction?

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.560
I'm going to say the Terminator.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.600
It's more succinct.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.700
Yeah. Yeah, one word to describe what you do, you know?

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:53.240
Engine of Destruction sounds like you're trying too hard to have like a really intimidating name.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.040
Engine of Destruction sounds like a part inside the Terminator's robotic body.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.980
You know, like, oh, now we got to install the Engine of Destruction.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.100
That's true, yeah.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:10.580
And this is not what I expect an Engine of Destruction to look like because there's just some weird design,

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:26.380
maybe musings on my own behalf that I had when I look at the box art and then the game, like, graphics, and then the, like, anime style, you know, in the menu when you pause.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:32.460
It's like an anime rendition of the Engine of Destruction, otherwise known as Billy Big Bang Blitz.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.380
He has, like, three different kinds of looks here.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.140
He's got the one on the back of the box that makes him look pretty fierce.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:44.020
Then in the game, I don't know, he's got like, he looks kind of like a Super Mario Brothers cutesy style character.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.920
And then when you pause, you get like this beautiful, like, portrait headshot and pixel art of him.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.880
So, not really sure which art style I'm supposed to interpret as.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Am I supposed to imagine the box art the entire time I'm playing the game?

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.360
Or am I supposed to feel like I'm more like in a cute, silly world like Super Mario Brothers?

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:11.620
I'm gonna go with the sort of close up during dialogue and when you pause, like, that's the canon look.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:19.720
And, you know, when you zoom out and you're playing the actual game, like, that's just the closest they could get to make it look correct.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:27.160
And the other thing was probably just, they hired a box art guy and he's like,

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:30.500
Yeah, we're trying to make a game with a guy that looks like this.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:33.360
And I'd never seen what they were actually trying to make.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:34.820
And he'd get Fabio. Yeah, and he'd get Fabio like that.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.880
So, I think that's what's going on.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:47.140
Um, yeah, I felt that the sprite, you know, to the best of most games, like, nicely represented what I imagined.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:53.320
Like, I can easily imagine that sprite as the guy in the pause menu or like the pixel art version.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.660
Yeah. I didn't even see the box art, so I don't know.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.260
It's pretty out there.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.360
I can, I figure it as such.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.240
And are you allowed to have two nicknames?

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:10.080
Are you allowed to be Billy Big Bang Blitz and also the Engine of Destruction?

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.060
See, that's also a thing.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.580
Like, is that, that's what's actually on the back of the box?

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.360
Yeah, yeah. Because I don't, I mean, I didn't finish this game, but I don't remember.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.480
I don't ever think he's referred to it as such.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:30.580
Yeah. Again, I think whoever designed the box, both the ad copy and the art, like, they never played the game.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:31.980
Yeah, that would make sense.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:40.720
I mean, I also think that you are allowed to have two nicknames, but if they do not go together at all, such as Billy Big Bang.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.440
What is it? Billy Big Bang Blitz.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.560
I think Blitz is his last name.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.040
So, Big Bang. Billy Big Bang Blitz.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:51.360
That's just like fun and like, oh, he's a crazy out there guy and then the Engine of Destruction.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.860
I think they need to be a little more cohesive than that.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:04:00.280
Well, those are just like the two, like, he's kind of bipolar, he's got a couple different moods, so he'll either be big,

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.420
Yeah, don't make him angry.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.520
Big Bang, and he's cool and fun.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:14.460
And then Engine of Destruction is after he's had a few too many whiskeys and maybe his girlfriend, Amy or whatever his name, like that she won't like listen to him.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.300
You know, any kind of different combination of things.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:23.540
Fair enough. So, in the game, you control Billy Big Bang Blitz.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.560
I swear, it's not even like they don't make a big deal out of it.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.000
So, I'm going to stop making a big deal out of it.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:27.900
He's bang. I just think it's funny.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.400
Yeah, I just like that.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:44.540
Yeah, he is bang. Who is, you can, basically, you're playing a platforming adventure RPG crossover style game where even though it seems like it's a platforming game, first and foremost,

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:48.960
there are branching paths of over 40 routes that the player can take in the game.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:05:02.360
And the reason where the adventure part comes in is because throughout these routes, you'll find and talk to either NPCs or you'll find a shop or another location that like leads to a secret location to another place.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:09.340
All these things can be found on the routes, but you have to traverse these routes through the platforming stages.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:23.500
So, the game is kind of non-linear and, you know, you gain, you don't necessarily gain experience points, but you develop your inventory as you continue to play the game, visit shops, and acquire specific power-ups that you need later on in the game.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:30.720
You can choose any which way to start or to go and you're allowed to backtrack to visit stages you've already seen.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:40.100
So, I feel like if we really want to talk about this game, we kind of have to like divide it up into sections or maybe that's just a fun, neat way for me to get you guys to be more coherent.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:48.300
But I feel like if we start talking about it as a platformer, then as an adventure game, and last as an RPG, we'll cover more ground that way.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.400
I don't need you to make me more coherent, Mike.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:57.320
Well, you sound a little, you know, enraged by that, so maybe I'm...

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.460
Mike, I don't even understand what you're saying right now.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:00.560
Yeah, exactly.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:05.840
Maybe we should just move on and talk about the platforming of this game.

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:07.500
Yeah, whatever you want. Yeah.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.240
Well, you know, it's the main hook, right?

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:12.820
So, you're entering these levels and, you know, you choose your path.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:16.380
Most times you're given like two options, but sometimes you're even given as many as three.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:20.360
You choose your path based on the number that it provides you.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.020
Like, oh, going left is number five.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.060
Probably we're going to call it stage five or whatever.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:29.480
And then those levels are like half Mega Man, half...

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:39.000
Yeah, I think actually mostly like Mega Man style with a little bit of like that Castlevania II sense of like you can explore and talk to people too sometimes.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:44.320
Sometimes you're doing all that, but they're short little bursts of levels.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.660
They're not like full stages.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:56.140
So, when we say 40 stages, it's not like each stage is a five-minute endeavor and you must visit all stages to complete the game or something like that.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:01.140
So, forget about all the branching paths for a minute and all the other things you can see and do.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:06.940
Just as a platformer, how does Billy Big Bang Blitz perform?

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:16.040
I'll say that at first, not considering all the other stuff, just the way it moves, it did sort of throw me off a little bit.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:20.080
Because there are some weird things that bothered me.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:28.940
And again, in order to explain why this got better, you'll understand once we get more to the RPG part.

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:35.080
But there were like things where when you jump in the water, you're like already losing health if you go below it.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.840
But then things are shooting at you and the only way to dodge is to go below water.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.680
And there were like weird things like that.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:42.800
There's stuff where like you hit the top of the screen when you jump.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:52.100
So, if you're like up high and you try to jump, you bump into the like invisible ceiling of the screen rather than just kind of going up and through a little bit and then coming back down.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:56.240
Like little things like that felt a little jank and they got better over time.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:01.020
But like that's just my, that was just my initial impression of the platforming itself.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:05.900
Don't want that to like make anyone think that like I had a bad time the whole time.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.820
But at first I was like, what is going on?

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:15.520
Yeah, like at the base level of how Bang performs or just handles, it is very tight.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:18.240
Like you're, you'll, you'll have that one-to-one.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:27.380
There's not a lot of, uh, it's not sticky, um, like a lot of other platformers, especially early platformers.

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:38.360
Um, but he, his jump is very strange and, and just the arc and height of that jump, um, will, will lead to what Joe was talking about.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:51.480
Um, especially if you're anywhere beyond, like if, if you're playing anywhere beyond, uh, the top half of the screen, you're going to bump your head on the ceiling slash sky.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:09:02.320
Um, and, uh, you know, you've got a, you've got a projectile that you shoot and there's only, you can only have three of those on the screen at once.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:11.080
Otherwise you have to wait for them to kind of depopulate and that, that can sometimes cause some issues, but that's also something we've seen before a lot.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:22.300
Uh, just getting into the nitty gritty of that, like there are the, the one thing that I did like about him in terms of how he controls is he could move and crouch at the same time.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.800
That's something that we've complained about a lot in the past.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:28.980
Uh, so there's, he's got a lot of tools.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:31.980
He can also climb on walls if it's the right kind of wall.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:39.560
Uh, so he's got a lot of tools available to him, but like, there are some aspects of it that were a little head scratching.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:47.600
So to that too, I mean, I, this is one of the games that I, I guess I made the mistake of assuming it was straightforward enough when I turned it on that I didn't need to read the manual.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:51.320
And I think that that also, I mean, I'm assuming a lot of this stuff is explained in the manual.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:54.020
I kind of figured it out organically or from watching videos afterwards.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.140
But, uh, like I had no idea you can climb walls.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:10:00.980
I had no idea that there were like platforms you couldn't jump down through.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:04.200
And so I was like, why are all these levels just dead ends?

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:06.600
And like the, you know, none of that stuff's obviously explained in the game.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:11.180
So I probably should have read the manual first, but I think that also like was stuff I was missing.

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:15.900
Like all the stuff you could do that I was missing when I first played it and was like, what, what is this game?

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:22.160
Because I wasn't like noticing all like the, um, the other additions like that I didn't know were possible.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.440
There are also levels that are dead ends though.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.300
So that, that's true too.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:34.820
But I don't think I actually discovered those in my initial, um, in my initial play, you know, pickup of this game where I was like already hard on it.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:44.860
And I think going back to your point, Sean, about just how bang controls and everything, I'd say the base version of bang, the one you start the game with is not a great start for this game.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:54.320
The, the upgrades, which are obviously meant to feel like, you know, rewarding power-ups that you've earned by killing enemies and buying them either at the shop or getting them elsewhere.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:57.160
Um, you know, they're meant to feel like actual improvements.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:04.820
I just think that the, the base version of bang where he just has his standard out, uh, load out and just the gun, the handgun.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.880
Um, it's, it's not that great.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:14.100
And the levels themselves are designed with a bit of like claustrophobia, uh, you know, both because of how the platforming works.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:18.500
So the, the platforms themselves, you guys were talking about hitting the ceiling and that's not great either.

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:27.600
You should be able to kind of float up there or something at the very least, but the platforms, it's almost, uh, it's cave-like in its design sometimes too.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:32.020
And I feel like certain enemies, just the way they're placed and everything.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.260
It's a lot of, uh, it's not a, it's not a fast moving game.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:43.400
Sometimes you do have to like shoot from afar, clear out the area and then go, or sometimes you have to take the hit and, you know, and just power through it too,

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.340
which is not, those aren't great feelings.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:48.420
I think it'd be a lot better if this game was just a little more open.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:54.440
Maybe if, if the size of everything was just shrink down a little bit, so this way they had more room.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:59.940
Uh, I, I feel like I, I kept running into that issue with the hit boxes, uh, in specific.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:09.940
Yeah. There's, um, it's, it's not specifically you one-to-one controlling the character, but I think it still falls into the same, uh, category.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:13.720
But also your power, your health.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:26.180
The way that it tracks that, um, you'll get however many little squares of health and one might intuit that, that means that you have three or four hits until you fall.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:27.320
That is not true.

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:39.360
Uh, each one is kind of invisibly subdivided into other hits that I think maybe some, uh, enemies do more damage than most.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:46.600
I never actually tested that theory, but, uh, you will take damage and you don't really know you're taking damage because your power doesn't go down.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:13:01.400
Um, and especially with how, uh, weirdly shaped your hit box seems to be, uh, you, you know, you're taking damage just because of like that tactile response, but you're not seeing it reflected on your power meter.

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:06.420
A lot of this can confuse and just make it not feel perfect.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:14.000
Yeah, it almost felt like some of those like power, like the, the different sections in your power meter felt almost like arbitrary.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:21.640
I swear sometimes I would, I would lose, I would lose the health immediately on first hit and then other times it would take like 10 hits or something.

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:29.400
I mean, maybe it was because maybe that first bar wasn't full and there's just no way of telling that, but like, it always looked like sometimes like one hit would kill me.

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:40.080
And then other times, uh, you would have, it's hard to get a handle on your relative safety because you're not really sure when that's going to happen.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:14:04.220
And also to your, to your point earlier, Mike, about, um, I know we're not really talking about upgrades that yet, but a lot of the upgrades will, will, we will see when we talk about them are more so like fixing problems with the way the game handles more so than giving you, uh, additional fun stuff.

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:15.100
Uh, the, the, the jet pack I will say is just fun and it's not fixing any problems, but like, uh, what, when it seems that they're more just, oh, I don't have to deal with this annoyance anymore.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.900
Uh, that, that seems like poor design in my opinion.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:32.720
Right. I keep thinking about, uh, you know, some of the best platformers and the super Mario brothers games when you, uh, die in that game and, or when you have to restart it because there's no save, you have to start all the way back at world one, one.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:40.100
And it's not really, uh, it's not a chore to then get through those levels again, because they're designed in a way that's just kind of fun to play them.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:50.080
Like, I don't think clash of demon had really had that for me as individual stages, the actual, uh, journey and adventure part that we'll get to in a second.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.520
That's all, that's what enhances the game.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:15:02.220
But yeah, if you actually just think about the fact that you have to sometimes visit these stages again, especially if you, uh, might've went the wrong way or now you need to, um, you know, you hit a dead end and you have to replay.

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:05.460
I, I'm not saying you have to go back and play like seven levels that you just beat again.

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:11.840
I'm not being that extreme, but you know, there is some backtracking in this and you're just playing these short platforming levels again.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:15.500
I don't think, uh, it's more of a slog to then get through them again.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:23.280
There was nothing like these levels maybe could have been more unique or more, uh, inspired, uh, or easier to get around.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.400
So this way, uh, backtracking wasn't that, uh, big of a deal.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:32.140
So I, I think they, they could have done more here, uh, to, to increase the feel of exploration.

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:39.660
Yeah. I think that this is where we often have different like tolerances for backtracking because you're right.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:49.580
I mean, everything you said, I agree with just for me, the levels were short enough that it was like, it never was like that didn't even really cross my mind because it always just felt like, Oh, okay.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.740
I got to go back this way. I'm familiar with this area now.

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:52.680
So like, that's kind of cool.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:53.680
I know where I'm going.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:57.960
I know where I got to get once I was like getting to the point where I'm backtracking a lot.

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:03.420
Um, but yeah, I mean, I think it's just, it doesn't bother me when there are short bouts of it like that.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:11.480
And I think it, it solves its own problem because if, if it were like this for the entire game, that would be a big problem.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:20.500
But, uh, once you kind of get the power up for teleportation, um, a lot of that kind of goes by the wayside.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:31.780
Right. You think about a game like dragon quest where you're constantly going back to the, um, to the, to the main town to report to the king and even save your game there.

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:46.880
Uh, if each one of those like trips back was, you know, like multiple levels that you had to keep traversing to, and you had to have bang, keep going back to like where you started to then like get the next mission or something that would be a train wreck of a game.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:50.000
So I do agree that the, the levels are short and that's enough.

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:52.740
Um, it's enough to tolerate them.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:17:01.380
I, I just, I guess I can't get over that idea that, you know, they could have, they could have been a little more unique even just if it didn't feel like a stage five.

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:06.800
And, you know, I don't know, then stage 13 or something, cause they don't, they're not sequential, the numbers on the route.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:09.800
Uh, so sometimes you'll be on stage five and move over to stage 13.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:17.920
It just felt like I was just doing another version of the same level rather than like, oh, this is how the route changed and evolved, blah, blah, blah.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:27.780
Yeah. And as far as the routes too, and sorry, I, I just the, the arbitrary order that we're talking about it, it just happens to be like all the negative things I have to say about the game.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:30.520
I do have good things to say about the game too, but the, the route.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:37.580
Like, it's great that they gave you a map and everything, but without there being numbers on the map, like, it just, it seems like such a small thing.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:42.040
Like so many NPCs will say like, oh, go to route seven and do this or whatever.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.480
And then I look at the map and it's like, okay, it's just a bunch of dots on a page.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:47.000
Like, there's, there's like, what are there, like 40 of them?

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:48.860
Like, like, I don't remember which one is which.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.340
Well, that's where I just wish.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:58.460
I think a lot of our listeners and just, you know, people that grew up with these games would tell you that you have to make your own map with your own label.

00:17:58.480 --> 00:17:59.400
I get that.

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:00.600
Yeah. And that's what I did.

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.480
I don't agree that that should be necessary, but.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:10.480
Yeah. That's what I did, but it just felt like there, why, why the map almost, I mean, the map almost felt arbitrary.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:13.260
