00:27:37.060 --> 00:27:40.560
And then you have to kind of piece together why you're not progressing.

00:27:40.560 --> 00:27:43.760
I think little things like that take this game.

00:27:43.780 --> 00:27:46.800
And that's why it's not just a platformer.

00:27:46.900 --> 00:28:00.580
It's not just a Super Mario Brothers Mega Man style game, because there is this style of fetch quests where you'll be told, oh, you need to get this thing or you need to do this thing in order to progress.

00:28:00.920 --> 00:28:04.720
Things are things are gated off in a way that they aren't in traditional platformers.

00:28:04.720 --> 00:28:13.660
Yeah, like there's an economy and inventory management and several different variations of upgrades.

00:28:13.660 --> 00:28:24.500
